{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<pitch>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLPitch","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPitch"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPitchV"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Music","anchor":"Music","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound"]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/init(step:alter:octave:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/alter","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/octave","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/step"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pitch is represented as a combination of the step of the diatonic scale, the chromatic alteration, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"octave."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Equatable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch/octave":{"type":"topic","title":"octave","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/octave","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch\/octave","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The octave of the pitch."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"octave"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MXLOctave","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOctaveV"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}],"title":"MXLSound","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSound","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSound","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Copyable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDirection":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A direction is a musical indication that is not necessarily attached to a specific note. Two or more may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to indicate words followed by the start of a dashed line, the end of a wedge followed by dynamics,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"etc. For applications where a specific direction is indeed attached to a specific note, the direction element"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection","title":"MXLDirection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLRest":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlrest","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLRest","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The rest element indicates notated rests or silences. Rest elements are usually empty, but placement on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staff can be specified using display-step and display-octave elements. If the measure attribute is set to yes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this indicates this is a complete measure rest."}],"title":"MXLRest","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLRest","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLRest","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/SH":{"title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch/step":{"type":"topic","title":"step","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/step","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch\/step","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The diatonic step of the pitch."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"step","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStep","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStepO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch/Equatable-Implementations":{"kind":"article","title":"Equatable Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/Equatable-Implementations","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch\/equatable-implementations","role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch/init(step:alter:octave:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"init(step:alter:octave:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/init(step:alter:octave:)","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLPitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch\/init(step:alter:octave:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"step","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStep","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLStepO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSemitones","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"octave","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOctave","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLOctaveV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAttributes":{"title":"MXLAttributes","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlattributes","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The attributes element contains musical information that typically changes on measure boundaries. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"includes key and time signatures, clefs, transpositions, and staving. When attributes are changed mid-measure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it affects the music in score order, not in MusicXML document order."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAttributes","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAttributes"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFullNote":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfullnote","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The full-note group is a sequence of the common note elements between cue\/grace notes and regular (full)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notes: pitch, chord, and rest information, but not duration (cue and grace notes do not have duration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoded). Unpitched elements are used for unpitched percussion, speaking voice, and other musical elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lacking determinate pitch."}],"title":"MXLFullNote","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFullNote","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFullNote","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch/alter":{"kind":"symbol","title":"alter","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch\/alter","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The chromatic alteration of the pitch, in semitones (e.g. "},{"code":"-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for flat, "},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for sharp)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch\/alter","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"alter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSemitones","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLSemitonesa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","title":"MXLNote","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPitch":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPitch","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPitch","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpitch","abstract":[{"text":"Pitch is represented as a combination of the step of the diatonic scale, the chromatic alteration, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"octave.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMusicItem":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMusicItem","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMusicItem","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for a music item."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmusicitem","type":"topic","title":"MXLMusicItem","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMusicItem","kind":"symbol"}}}